  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ac41192c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Compare user activity measures\n",
    "\n",
    "To better understand the most active accounts, I combine the number of distinct albums with the total number of listens for each user.\n",
    "\n",
    "This shows that the extreme users are not all unusual in the same way. Some have very broad listening histories across tens of thousands of albums, while others have extremely high listen counts relative to the number of distinct albums. These users should therefore be investigated before deciding on a filtering rule."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "edf6afe7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Investigate extreme users\n",
    "\n",
    "The previous results show a sharp jump in activity at the very top of the distribution. I therefore examine how many users exceed several high thresholds for distinct albums and total listens.\n",
    "\n",
    "This helps determine whether the most extreme accounts represent a very small fraction of the dataset and whether an upper activity filter would be appropriate before modelling."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "id": "1b3abc8b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Users with > 500 albums: 38 (0.196%)\n",
      "Users with > 1,000 albums: 30 (0.155%)\n",
      "Users with > 2,000 albums: 25 (0.129%)\n",
      "Users with > 5,000 albums: 16 (0.083%)\n",
      "Users with > 10,000 albums: 6 (0.031%)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "thresholds = [500, 1000, 2000, 5000, 10000]\n",
    "\n",
    "for threshold in thresholds:\n",
    "    n_users = (albums_per_user > threshold).sum()\n",
    "    percentage = n_users / len(albums_per_user) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(\n",
    "        f\"Users with > {threshold:,} albums: \"\n",
    "        f\"{n_users:,} ({percentage:.3f}%)\"\n",
    "    )"
   ]
  },
