   "source": [
    "### Listening intensity among highly active users\n",
    "\n",
    "The most active users vary considerably in how frequently they listen to each album. Some users have very broad histories with relatively few listens per album, while others combine broad listening histories with high repeat listening.\n",
    "\n",
    "The extreme users therefore do not appear to follow one obviously invalid pattern. Rather than removing them solely because they are highly active, I will treat them cautiously and assess the effect of any upper-user filtering on the modelling dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c047925d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Inspect album sparsity\n",
    "\n",
    "After examining unusually active users, the next step is to look at the dataset from the album side.\n",
    "\n",
    "Collaborative filtering depends on overlap between users, so I examine how many distinct users have interacted with each album. If most albums are associated with only one user, they provide little information for learning similarities between listeners.\n",
    "\n",
    "This section therefore measures the number of users per album and identifies how much of the catalogue has enough shared interaction to be useful for modelling."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "id": "728e5714",
